  "completed_components": {
    "selection_and_collision": "Exact one/two-point subset sampling bounds; collision-relation embedding into the full stacked relation space; actual arithmetic collision probability and selected pair mass.",
    "literal_finite_mask": "Every fixed dictionary is compared first on each prime fibre. Averaged deleted source cost is exactly a*#bad. The finite bound is 2*a*D+8*a^2*#mask*B+6*a^2*edges+2*a*p*R, retaining the actual sparse mask size.",
    "uniform_typical_rate": "The supremum of admissible actual mean distances defines one bounded nonnegative r_N. A logarithmic envelope proves the literal uniform o(nu) remainder. The same r_N controls the exceptional proportion, every deterministic readout and the infinite iid comparison with exact remainder 8*Lambda^2*B/N.",
    "information_root": "Existence of the actual information root on [V,Vhat], uniqueness, endpoint values, strict antitonicity, constrained maximum and strict improvement. No implicit derivative or root-existence premise.",
    "information_limit": "Exact quadratic identity and parameter squeezing imply the displayed limit (sqrt(theta^2+8)-3*theta)/4 for the actual information budget divided by V.",
    "information_field": "Literal proposition 6.2: all sites, signs and unbounded excesses at the information-adapted full prime sigma-algebra. The explicit rate is 67*exp(-cprime*nu)+64*N^(-1/3+epsilon). Support band is derived; all deterministic readouts contract.",
